This repo is **Kuala Lepak**, a non-violent GTA-style Malaysian life game (Next.js 16 +
React Three Fiber). Before touching the city, the hub or Anne Maju's room, read
**`docs/CITY_V2.md`** (how the city is generated and the rules that stop overlaps and
collision bugs). For product vision and roadmap see `docs/KUALA_LEPAK.md`. Key rules:

- Never type a world coordinate into a component: everything placed comes from `src/city/plan`.
- No coplanar faces (z-fighting) and no visibly intersecting merged parts; follow the y-layer table in `docs/CITY_V2.md`.
- Vehicles only exist in `src/city/sim/traffic.ts`; keep its seeded tests green.

- Never use drei `<Html>`; use the projected DOM overlay pattern.
- Cache canvas textures at module level; never create textures per mount.
- Per-frame simulation state lives outside React (module objects read in `useFrame`).
- Respect the strict React Compiler lint rules (no randomness/time in render, no setState in effects, no ref access in render).
- All player-facing text in BM and EN string tables; parody names for real brands/landmarks; non-violent content.
- Bump the game version in `meta.ts` and add a `CHANGELOG.md` entry for player-facing changes.
- The city is generated from `src/city/plan` (grid → roads, lots, props, lanes, colliders). Add new buildings, props or roads to the plan, never by hand in a scene; render code is in `src/city/kit` and `src/city/components`.
- Run `pnpm check:layout` after changing the plan (overlaps, reachability, traffic sim). Fix the plan; don't loosen the tests.
- No religious buildings. Delivery and ride brands are parodies (GRAP, SHOPI, foodpandai, LALAMOOV), never real names.
- Run `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit && pnpm lint && pnpm build` before pushing (build runs the tests).
